            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The price of a new boat is $28 000. It depreciates by 20% of its value each year.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find how long it will take for the boat to depreciate to $11000. Answer to the nearest year.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "4 years",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}S&=V_0(1-r)^n\\\\11000&=28000(1-0.2)^n\\\\0.8^n&=\\frac{11000}{28000}\\\\n&=\\frac{\\log(11000/28000)}{\\log(0.8)}\\end{align*}$$\nThis is approximately $4.19$ years, so the time is **4 years**, to the nearest year.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
